window.LEONIDA_DATA = {"game":"Grand Theft Auto VI","platform":"PlayStation 5","list":"the official 55 trophies","counts":{"platinum":1,"gold":2,"silver":6,"bronze":46},"kinds":{"story":"Story & missions","completion":"100% / collection","freeform":"Freeform & activities","hidden":"Unclear (hidden hint)"},"road":[{"title":"Opening and Chapter 1: learn the map, take the postcards","ids":[2,3,44],"text":"Finish Gone Fishing and Chapter 1 at a normal pace, and on the first drive along the coast stop for the Ocean Beach cocktail. Nothing is missable yet; this is where you start the habit of reading the trophy list."},{"title":"Chapter 2: the collection habits begin","ids":[4,48,31],"text":"Chapter 2 is where collectibles and choices start counting. Begin WAiNK It stops along your routes (100 locations is a marathon, start early) and make your story choices deliberately rather than reloading around them."},{"title":"Chapter 3: the map opens, activities go on the list","ids":[5,16,20,21,45,55,19],"text":"When Chapter 3 finishes and the state opens up, do Master of None's nine activity types, register vehicles in Scooter Bros, and start winning races. The activity pass carries the fishing challenge against Cal and the arcade game alongside it. Keep one showroom breakout (Capital Offense) for a planned session."},{"title":"Chapter 4 and free roam: stunts, vehicles, the one-time set-ups","ids":[15,35,18,49,51,46,33,34,39,40],"text":"This is the freeform block before the story turns: 250 stunts, 100 vehicles discovered, the 14 Top Fun drone races, the shops and bank pass, and the jewelry store. Plan the two partner trophies (Hot Together, Retail Therapy) and the undetected robbery as deliberate attempts of their own."},{"title":"Mid-game strands: finish your contacts","ids":[8,9,10,11,12,13,22,23,24,26,27,29,25],"text":"Every contact strand on the list completes at its final mission, so work them as they come and close eight of them (Strangers & Freaks). The story missions in this block come with the campaign; Trust, Break the Bank and the rest need nothing extra once you finish each one."},{"title":"Weapons and the range","ids":[17,36],"text":"With the campaign's weapons in hand, take the 42 Shooting Range golds in batches, and set up one crowded Combat Focus fight on purpose for Gunslinger."},{"title":"The airport and the tank: the planned set-pieces","ids":[37,38,41],"text":"After VCIA Takedown the airport is familiar ground: stage the unscheduled departure, and read a community video for Challenging Tank's exact spot, then do it with armour and patience. Add one armoured truck robbery with a clean escape."},{"title":"Story close: finish Chapters 4 and the final mission","ids":[6,7,14],"text":"Before the final mission, open the 100% screen and clear the list of anything still open, because this is the natural break between the campaign and the cleanup. Complete Chapter 4 and the final mission, and A Long Road should be within reach of the last freeform entries."},{"title":"Cleanup: meditate, launder, build the garages, finish the map","ids":[28,32,42,43,30,52,53,54,47,50],"text":"A dedicated sweep: all 18 meditation spots, the 52 areas, nine gang operations, three card sets, the garage purchases and shop spending, the laundering total, and the two hidden moments (Personal Best, The Truth Is Out There) on the free-roam routes."},{"title":"The last trophies: the platinum","ids":[1],"text":"With every other trophy earned, Vice Got a Price! arrives by itself. If it does not, the game's trophy list names the one still open."}],"flags":[{"id":33,"name":"Hot Together","why":"Four stars with your partner aboard, lost together. Split the escape and the setup resets."},{"id":34,"name":"Retail Therapy","why":"Three shops in a row without the Wanted Level clearing. Every star change in between breaks the chain."},{"id":36,"name":"Gunslinger","why":"Five takedowns in one Combat Focus. The timer is short: set the fight up in advance."},{"id":37,"name":"Catch Me If You Can","why":"One unscheduled take-off from VCIA: a failed escape restarts at the terminal."},{"id":39,"name":"Sneakthief","why":"No detection at all in the jewelry store: one sighting is one failure."},{"id":45,"name":"Capital Offense","why":"A breakout in style through a showroom: it is the style that is checked, so plan the exit."},{"id":38,"name":"Challenging Tank","why":"A hidden tank encounter: a planned fight, not a chance one. A video guide has the exact condition."},{"id":49,"name":"Bad Luck, I Guess","why":"The second attempt is the charm: retry a failure deliberately rather than reloading around it."},{"id":50,"name":"The Truth Is Out There","why":"A strange sighting on the state's remote roads at night: keep free-roam time for it."}],"trophies":[{"id":1,"grade":"platinum","name":"Vice Got a Price!","description":"Congratulations! You're a Leonida Legend.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":9,"guide":"The platinum. It unlocks last, automatically, once every one of the other 54 is on the shelf - there is nothing extra to do for it, so treat it as the finish line rather than a task. My tip: before the final missions, sweep the freeform list (stunts, activities, robberies, collectibles) so the platinum lands the moment both golds do.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Congratulations! You're a Leonida Legend.\""},{"id":2,"grade":"bronze","name":"Just Like Paradise","description":"Complete Gone Fishing.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":1,"guide":"Opening mission of the game. Complete Gone Fishing once it is offered: the first mission of the story, so it cannot be missed, and it is the one that hands you the controls and points at the next chapter. Missable: no - the mission only moves forward once you finish it.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete Gone Fishing.\""},{"id":3,"grade":"bronze","name":"Paradise Lost","description":"Complete Chapter 1.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":2,"guide":"Story trophy for closing Chapter 1, the first chapter after the opening mission. Just play the main missions in order; the trophy pops with the chapter's last mission. Missable: no: chapters are part of the main path.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete Chapter 1.\""},{"id":4,"grade":"bronze","name":"T**s Ass Drug Money","description":"Complete Chapter 2.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":3,"guide":"Story trophy for closing Chapter 2. The chapter's missions are all main-line, so it comes with progress. Nothing to do afterwards. Missable: no.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete Chapter 2.\""},{"id":5,"grade":"bronze","name":"Vice City, Baby!","description":"Complete Chapter 3.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":4,"guide":"Story trophy for closing Chapter 3. A useful checkpoint: its mission set is where the state opens up, so it is a good moment to detour into freeform trophies before the pace of the story picks up. Missable: no.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete Chapter 3.\""},{"id":6,"grade":"bronze","name":"Top Of The World, Ma","description":"Complete Chapter 4.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":5,"guide":"Story trophy for closing Chapter 4, the last chapter before the final mission. If a trophy on the list is still open and it lives in a part of the world the story is about to leave behind, this is the last comfortable point to go back for it. Missable: no.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete Chapter 4.\""},{"id":7,"grade":"gold","name":"You Gotta Know When to Get Off","description":"Complete the final mission.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":8,"guide":"The story's finish. It comes after Chapter 4 and before the 100% cleanup, so everything you still want from the map has to be done during the campaign or in free roam afterwards (free roam stays open, but the story's own mission strands do not rewind). Missable: no: it is on the main path.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete the final mission.\""},{"id":8,"grade":"bronze","name":"Trust","description":"Complete Breakfast Run.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"A story mission named Breakfast Run, completed as part of the campaign. Take it when it is offered, and see it through: missions inside the story do not fail permanently, but they do stop showing up until you finish them, which stalls the chapter. Missable: no.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete Breakfast Run.\""},{"id":9,"grade":"bronze","name":"Break the Bank","description":"Complete The Cartel Heist.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"The Cartel Heist is a story heist. Heists are plan-then-do missions, so before you start the final part, put the rest of the list in a state where nothing rides on the crew or your loadout. Missable: no.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete The Cartel Heist.\""},{"id":10,"grade":"bronze","name":"Family Matters","description":"Complete Child's Play.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"Story mission Child's Play. It sits in the main mission chain, so it arrives on its own while you push the story. Missable: no.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete Child's Play.\""},{"id":11,"grade":"bronze","name":"DWNFALL","description":"Complete Headliners.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"Story mission Headliners. Play it in order with the rest of its chapter. Missable: no.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete Headliners.\""},{"id":12,"grade":"bronze","name":"Hi-Jacked","description":"Complete VCIA Takedown.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":7,"guide":"The story mission VCIA Takedown, set at the airport area of the state. Once you are on this stretch of the story, it is also the right time to chase the two airport trophies on this list that you can set up yourself: Catch Me If You Can and A Classic Blitz Play. Missable: no.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete VCIA Takedown.\""},{"id":13,"grade":"bronze","name":"Snow Storm","description":"Complete Operation Savage Glory.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"Story mission Operation Savage Glory. It is a set-piece, so bring the good weapons and body armour; failing it just restarts it, the trophy is not at risk. Missable: no.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete Operation Savage Glory.\""},{"id":14,"grade":"gold","name":"A Long Road","description":"Attain 100% Completion.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":9,"guide":"The completion gold, and the real long haul: 100% of the list the game's pause menu tracks. Build it up as you play rather than save it all for after the story: every stunt, race, activity, collectible and robbery on this list feeds the meter. Before the final missions, open the completion list and note exactly what is left, so nothing depends on a strand that closes with the campaign.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Attain 100% Completion.\""},{"id":15,"grade":"silver","name":"Cunning Stunts","description":"Complete 250 Stunts.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":4,"guide":"250 stunts, counted as you free-roam: jumps, spins, near misses, the moves the game counts for the meter. Nothing here is one-time, so it can be pumped across the whole map at any point. Fast route: a few favourite loops of long jumps and ramps with a fast car or bike, repeated in free roam with each stunt counting toward the 250.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete 250 Stunts.\""},{"id":16,"grade":"bronze","name":"Master of None","description":"Try each type of activity once.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":5,"guide":"The activity types are the nine groups on offer across the state (the same nine the game's activity filter lists). Play each one once and the trophy is yours. Because it is one pass per type, it fits neatly beside the chapter-3 point where the map opens up: take the list of types and tick them off between missions.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Try each type of activity once.\""},{"id":17,"grade":"silver","name":"The Shootist","description":"Earn a gold medal in all Shooting Range challenges.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"42 Shooting Range challenges, each gold. Gold is the top medal of each challenge, so expect repeated clean runs: the reliable route is to learn one challenge at a time, then chain them. Do the range early enough to have the run of it, but after you own the weapons the range's loadout can offer.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Earn a gold medal in all Shooting Range challenges.\""},{"id":18,"grade":"bronze","name":"Top Fun","description":"Win a Top Fun Drone Race at every location.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":5,"guide":"Top Fun drone races run at 14 locations. It is a win at each, not a finish, so learn each course before you race it for real: the drone is twitchy and the courses are tight. Nothing is scored here because of the story, so any order works.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Win a Top Fun Drone Race at every location.\""},{"id":19,"grade":"bronze","name":"Earn Cash, Not Kudos","description":"Win 20 different races.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":4,"guide":"Twenty different races, each a win: not twenty attempts at the same one. Mix street, water and dirt races for variety; the 'different' is the point, so keep a note of which ones you have won if you play across several sessions (this app's notes box, or the game's own race counters, work).","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Win 20 different races.\""},{"id":20,"grade":"bronze","name":"Baited My Tackle","description":"Beat Cal in a fishing challenge.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":5,"guide":"A fishing challenge against Cal. Fishing is one of the activities the freeform list counts, so this can land on the same pass as the fishing spots you visit for the collectible strands around the state. Beat Cal once and it is done; it is repeatable, so a bad run costs nothing.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Beat Cal in a fishing challenge.\""},{"id":21,"grade":"bronze","name":"Stick Fiddler","description":"Complete an arcade game.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":5,"guide":"One arcade game, finished: it is the single sit-down cabinet that counts, not every one in the state. Locate an arcade cabinet in the city, learn its pattern and play it through in one sitting. A short, low-risk stop on any free-roam sweep.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete an arcade game.\""},{"id":22,"grade":"bronze","name":"Road to Rehabilitation","description":"Complete the final mission for Andy.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"Andy's final mission in a stranger/contact strand. Strands build up in steps, so finish each character's missions as they appear: the last one in a strand only unlocks after every earlier one is done. Finishing them late is fine as long as the strand stays open after the campaign. Missable: the description gives no one-time window; treat each contact's strand as finish-it-when-you-can.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete the final mission for Andy.\""},{"id":23,"grade":"bronze","name":"This Was No Boat Accident","description":"Complete the final mission for Kenton.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"Kenton's final mission, the sea-side contact strand of the state. Same rule as the other contacts here: do each step as it comes so the final mission is reachable. Missable: not on the official description; a strand left half done is a chore, not a loss.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete the final mission for Kenton.\""},{"id":24,"grade":"bronze","name":"The Lone Rider","description":"Complete the final mission for Billy.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"Billy's final mission. Billy's strand is one of the contact missions chains, and the last one needs the rest of it done first. Bring a fast bike: the name is a hint about the chase. Missable: no window named by the official description.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete the final mission for Billy.\""},{"id":26,"grade":"bronze","name":"Supply & Demand","description":"Complete the final mission for Randy.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"Randy's final mission. Finish the earlier steps of Randy's strand when they appear, then close it with this one. Missable: no window named.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete the final mission for Randy.\""},{"id":27,"grade":"bronze","name":"Spin On This!","description":"Complete the final mission for Tyrone.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"Tyrone's final mission. As with the other contacts, the last mission of the chain arrives after the chain's earlier steps. Play it with a stunt-ready car in mind: the name fits the stunt counter. Missable: no window named.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete the final mission for Tyrone.\""},{"id":25,"grade":"silver","name":"Strangers & Freaks","description":"Complete 8 mission strands for strangers across the state of Leonida.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":7,"guide":"Eight complete stranger strands, out of the many the state offers. A strand is only complete at its final mission, so this trophy rewards the finisher, not the tourist. Pick eight characters early in the campaign, finish their chains, and the count comes to you naturally by chapter 4. Missable: no, as long as you keep going back to the contacts.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete 8 mission strands for strangers across the state of Leonida.\""},{"id":28,"grade":"bronze","name":"Positive Mental Attitude","description":"Meditate at every spot across Leonida.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"Meditation spots, 18 of them, all across the state. This is a map sweep: the spots are marked as you get close, so a drive around the coast roads and the hill country, hopping out where the prompt appears, is the fastest way to collect all 18. Check the list before you leave thinking you had them all.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Meditate at every spot across Leonida.\""},{"id":29,"grade":"bronze","name":"Fair Game","description":"Hunt a unique animal for Bret.","kind":"story","kindLabel":"Story & missions","missable":false,"phase":5,"guide":"A one-off hunt for Bret: find and take the unique animal the mission asks for. Hunting is its own activity, so it also counts toward the activities pass. Bret's mission stays on the map, so a missed animal costs patience, not the trophy. Missable: no window named by the official description.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Hunt a unique animal for Bret.\""},{"id":30,"grade":"silver","name":"Don't Touch My Deck","description":"Complete 3 Collectible Card sets.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":7,"guide":"Three complete collectible card sets. Card sets are one of the state's collection systems: each needs a set's worth of cards from around the map, not just one card. Pick three sets near the areas the story visits and finish them one at a time; the cards you find outside those sets still feed the 100% meters.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete 3 Collectible Card sets.\""},{"id":31,"grade":"silver","name":"You WAiNKer!","description":"WAiNK It at 100 locations.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":3,"guide":"WAiNK It, the phone app-like pastime, at 100 different locations. That is a lot of stops, so tie each one to a trip you were making anyway: a location on every route through the city and the map adds up by itself. The app marks the ones already done, so check before starting a sweep.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"WAiNK It at 100 locations.\""},{"id":32,"grade":"bronze","name":"One Last Thing","description":"Complete 50 Challenges.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":7,"guide":"Fifty challenges, the kind the state's list keeps as short tasks (racing, stunt and activity side tasks). This overlaps heavily with everything else on the list, so do not chase it alone: it grows while you complete races, stunts and activities. Its count is visible on the challenges screen.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Complete 50 Challenges.\""},{"id":33,"grade":"bronze","name":"Hot Together","description":"Lose a 4 star Wanted Level with your partner and escape the heat.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":true,"phase":7,"guide":"A two-step window: reach a four-star Wanted Level with your partner in the same car or group, then lose it together, never apart. Going down or splitting up resets the setup, so this is a deliberate session rather than a side effect of story chaos. Do it in a stolen fast car with a garage or tunnel route to hide in. Missable: yes, one setup, one escape, no partial credit.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Lose a 4 star Wanted Level with your partner and escape the heat.\""},{"id":34,"grade":"bronze","name":"Retail Therapy","description":"Rob 3 shops back-to-back with your partner without losing your Wanted Level.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":true,"phase":7,"guide":"Three shops in a row, partner aboard, and the Wanted Level must never clear between them. Every star change in between breaks the chain, so plan the three shops as a loop close together and let the level ride. Have a getaway car parked between each pair. Missable: yes: the chain only works unbroken.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Rob 3 shops back-to-back with your partner without losing your Wanted Level.\""},{"id":35,"grade":"bronze","name":"Whip It Good","description":"Discover 100 vehicles.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":4,"guide":"A hundred different vehicles discovered: each new model you get into counts once. Traffic hopping, car parks, the airport and the marina get you most of the way during ordinary play. A parked-car circuit of the city's car parks across a few sessions closes the gap, and you will see the count in the game's collections.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Discover 100 vehicles.\""},{"id":36,"grade":"bronze","name":"Gunslinger","description":"Take down 5 enemies in a single use of Combat Focus.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":true,"phase":6,"guide":"Five kills inside one Combat Focus: the ability runs on a short timer, so the five have to be close together and in sight. Set the fight up on purpose: a crowded street shootout, a doorway you back into cover and five slow, aimed shots. Waiting for this by accident is the usual mistake. Missable: yes: one activation, all five.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Take down 5 enemies in a single use of Combat Focus.\""},{"id":37,"grade":"bronze","name":"Catch Me If You Can","description":"Make an unscheduled departure at VCIA.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":true,"phase":7,"guide":"An unscheduled departure from VCIA: take an aircraft off the airport without the timetable's blessing. The window is the take-off: half-finished escapes end in a restart at the terminal with the Wanted Level still on you. Steal it at night or in a quiet slot, and clear the runway before you lift off. Missable: yes: one take-off to get right.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Make an unscheduled departure at VCIA.\""},{"id":40,"grade":"silver","name":"Maximum Withdrawal","description":"Rob 5 Bank Vaults and escape.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":7,"guide":"Five bank vault robberies, each ending in a clean escape. Unlike the shop chain, these can be done in any order and on different days; only the escape must close each one. Plan each bank's route out before you enter: the alarm brings the department, and a sandbox of police cars between you and the hideout is the usual failure.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Rob 5 Bank Vaults and escape.\""},{"id":41,"grade":"bronze","name":"A Classic Blitz Play","description":"Rob an Armored Truck and escape.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":7,"guide":"One armoured truck robbery with an escape. A single-event version of the bank list: stop the truck, take the cargo, get away. Its guard detail makes the approach the whole puzzle, and the escape is the same short chase the banks teach you. Can be attempted again if it goes wrong.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Rob an Armored Truck and escape.\""},{"id":42,"grade":"bronze","name":"The Goodtime State","description":"Explore all 52 areas of Leonida.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":9,"guide":"Fifty-two named areas of the state, each visited at least once. The areas are the state's districts and wild places; the map reveals them as you enter. A looping road trip around the coast and the inland roads at some point in the campaign gets almost all of them, and the story's missions fill most of the rest. The map's list shows what is still dark.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Explore all 52 areas of Leonida.\""},{"id":43,"grade":"bronze","name":"Pest Control","description":"Rob an Illegal Operation belonging to each gang.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":7,"guide":"One illegal operation per gang, for each of the nine gangs in the state. That is nine operations in nine different pieces of territory: keep a list, because the game's operations list does not group them that way. Each operation is a set-piece robbery, so pair them with the armoured trucks and bank runs as a single robbery pass.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Rob an Illegal Operation belonging to each gang.\""},{"id":38,"grade":"bronze","name":"Challenging Tank","description":"Kinda hot in these Rhinos.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":true,"phase":7,"guide":"A hidden trophy, and the official description is a hint, not a recipe: it points at a tank encounter with a very deliberate joke line. The reliable reading is that you need to be in a tight fight with tanks and come out of it alive. Armoured, patient and close: hit the tracks from behind cover. The exact trigger is the one thing this guide cannot state honestly from the official text alone; consult a community video walkthrough for the spot and the condition. Treat it as a one-time event you plan, not one you stumble into.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Kinda hot in these Rhinos.\""},{"id":39,"grade":"bronze","name":"Sneakthief","description":"Rob a jewelry store without being detected.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":true,"phase":7,"guide":"A jewelry store robbery with no detection at all: one camera sighting or one responding guard fails it. The route is the trophy: scout the shop's exits, take the staff outlet first, and disable the alarm before you touch a counter. A silenced approach and a mask. Missable: yes: detection is final for that attempt; retry by leaving and coming back fresh.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Rob a jewelry store without being detected.\""},{"id":44,"grade":"bronze","name":"In The Beginning…","description":"Enjoy a cocktail with a view on Ocean Beach.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":2,"guide":"A cocktail on Ocean Beach, from a spot with a view. The bars on that beachfront serve drinks in the evening; get one and lingering a few seconds does the rest. It is a postcard trophy and a good one to take on the first drive along the coast, when the story takes you past it anyway.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Enjoy a cocktail with a view on Ocean Beach.\""},{"id":45,"grade":"bronze","name":"Capital Offense","description":"Smash your way out of a vehicle showroom in classic style.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":true,"phase":3,"guide":"A showroom breakout: get a car out through a showroom, the old-fashioned way, in style. The style is the requirement: drive a car through the showroom's glass, not quietly reverse out through the back. Alert the staff with the noise you make, and have a fast car ready for the exit. Missable: yes: a clean breakout is the point, and a mess can fail the style.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Smash your way out of a vehicle showroom in classic style.\""},{"id":46,"grade":"bronze","name":"Let’s Go Bowling","description":"Follow-through at the Kolt & Associates' bowling alley.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":5,"guide":"A bowling alley tied to the Kolt & Associates name. Play a round to the end: 'follow-through' is the throw, so the trophy comes with one complete game, not with the visit. Bowling also feeds Master of None's activity pass and Ten Pin's melee variant, so plan the round beside a Ten Pin attempt.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Follow-through at the Kolt & Associates' bowling alley.\""},{"id":47,"grade":"bronze","name":"Personal Best","description":"A partnership with mass appeal.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":6,"guide":"A hidden trophy and a deliberately vague description: something a partnership of yours does with real mass appeal. Read it as a moment with your partner that the city notices: perform in front of a crowd (stunts, races or a public activity the game counts). Keep it in mind while you chase Cunning Stunts and the race wins; one of those public performances is what the trophy remembers.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"A partnership with mass appeal.\""},{"id":48,"grade":"bronze","name":"Actions Speak Louder","description":"Choices made (for better or worse).","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":7,"guide":"A hidden trophy about making choices. The game counts your choices (the trophy's tracker asks for 500), so this is not one decision but a sampling of them: story decisions and free-roam choices both count, and the numbers go up behind the scenes. Do not worry about the 'for better or worse' wording: the direction does not matter, only that choices are made.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Choices made (for better or worse).\""},{"id":49,"grade":"bronze","name":"Bad Luck, I Guess","description":"Second time's the charm.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":true,"phase":4,"guide":"A hidden, ironic trophy: the second attempt is the charm. It rewards coming back after a failure in the same place, so if a stunt, race or mission goes wrong, take the retry on purpose rather than reloading to undo it. Any repeat could catch it: my tip is to go back to a stunt you bailed on first and finish it, and to keep at a race you lost rather than leaving.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Second time's the charm.\""},{"id":50,"grade":"bronze","name":"The Truth Is Out There","description":"What the hell just happened?","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":true,"phase":6,"guide":"A hidden trophy about witnessing something strange: an event in the state that is out of the ordinary. These sightings are map events you can find, not story scenes; drive the state's remote roads at night and stop when the game shows you something unexplained. It is the most likely one to be dulled by rushing the story; keep the free-roam time for it. If you have not seen it by the campaign's end, a community map of the state's odd events will point you at the places without spoiling the story.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"What the hell just happened?\""},{"id":51,"grade":"bronze","name":"Ten Pin","description":"Bowl 'em over with a melee drive-by.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":5,"guide":"A bowling-joke trophy: knock somebody over with a melee drive-by, the kind of pass you deliver from a moving vehicle. It pairs perfectly with the bowling alley visit: the joke is the alley, the action is the street. One clean hit is enough, and it is repeatable, so a misses cost nothing.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Bowl 'em over with a melee drive-by.\""},{"id":52,"grade":"bronze","name":"Dime on the Dollar","description":"Earn $250,000 laundering Marked Bills through your contacts.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":8,"guide":"Two hundred and fifty thousand dollars of laundering, through your contacts, on Marked Bills. Marked bills come from robberies and come up in steady supply once your robbery pass is running, so this is a late-game money trophy rather than a detour: bank it as the robberies land and check the laundered total before the story's end.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Earn $250,000 laundering Marked Bills through your contacts.\""},{"id":53,"grade":"bronze","name":"Treat Yo Self","description":"Spend $100,000 across all shops.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":8,"guide":"Spend a hundred thousand in shops, which in practice means buying the things worth buying: car upgrades, clothing, weapons and properties feed the same counter. Track it against the completion total so your shop spending is part of the plan, not cash burnt in the wrong place.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Spend $100,000 across all shops.\""},{"id":54,"grade":"bronze","name":"Little Boxes","description":"Purchase all garage properties.","kind":"completion","kindLabel":"100% / collection","missable":false,"phase":8,"guide":"Every garage property in the state, eight of them. Property prices are the real requirement, so buy them as money comes in and treat it as the shop-spending arm of the completion plan: each garage also gives you a safe place to store the vehicles the other trophies need.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Purchase all garage properties.\""},{"id":55,"grade":"bronze","name":"On the Spot","description":"Register 10 vehicles to the Scooter Bros app.","kind":"freeform","kindLabel":"Freeform & activities","missable":false,"phase":4,"guide":"Ten vehicles registered in the Scooter Bros app. Registration is a menu chore, not a drive: open the app, register ten of the vehicles you already own or steal, and it is done. The vehicles you register count toward the 100 discovered as well, so this is a shortcut for Whip It Good's early count.","source":"Official PlayStation 5 description, quoted in the row: \"Register 10 vehicles to the Scooter Bros app.\""}]}
;
